#[navbar]

#[section, $md:
    @../ (Documentation) / Constants and compile-time behaviour

    # Constants and compile-time behaviour

    A constant tells the compiler to finish a value before runtime. Unlike a
    read-only runtime binding, a Moth constant can depend only on other
    compile-time values and must fold completely.

    The same rule covers scalar values, const records and templates. Direct const
    fragments can contribute finished content to an HTML page.
]

